---
/*
 * The same envelope at two hops. The task list is identical in both; only the
 * current-task index moves, and each service increments it. That is why no
 * service needs to know what comes after it, and why the pipeline is reordered
 * by changing the message rather than the code.
 *
 * Field labels are the descriptions from content-source, not invented JSON keys:
 * the source describes what the envelope carries without naming the keys.
 *
 * Shared canvas and styling: the .diagram rules in src/styles/global.css.
 */
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <div class="diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      viewBox="-8 -10 596 258"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="envelope-title envelope-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    >
      <title id="envelope-title">A self-describing message envelope at two pipeline hops</title>
      <desc id="envelope-desc">
        The same envelope is shown twice. Both copies carry an identical ordered task list of extract,
        translate, score and filter, plus per-service configuration, a target queue and exception and
        traceback fields. At the first hop the current index points at extract; after the document
        extraction service increments it, the index points at translate. Only the index changes.
      </desc>

      <g class="edge-label">
        <text x="0" y="0">identical either side, except one line</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Hop one. -->
      <g class="node">
        <rect x="0" y="20" width="228" height="146" rx="3" />
      </g>
      <g class="field">
        <text x="14" y="44">tasks: extract, translate,</text>
        <text x="14" y="64">score, filter</text>
        <text x="14" y="92">per-service config</text>
        <text x="14" y="112">target queue</text>
        <text x="14" y="132">exception / traceback</text>
      </g>
      <g class="accent">
        <text x="14" y="156">index -&gt; extract</text>
      </g>

      <!-- The broker carries it from one service to the next. -->
      <g class="collapse">
        <line x1="240" y1="93" x2="296" y2="93" />
        <polygon points="296,87 310,93 296,99" />
        <text x="275" y="81" text-anchor="middle">ActiveMQ</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Hop two: identical envelope, index advanced by one. -->
      <g class="node">
        <rect x="310" y="20" width="228" height="146" rx="3" />
      </g>
      <g class="field">
        <text x="324" y="44">tasks: extract, translate,</text>
        <text x="324" y="64">score, filter</text>
        <text x="324" y="92">per-service config</text>
        <text x="324" y="112">target queue</text>
        <text x="324" y="132">exception / traceback</text>
      </g>
      <g class="accent">
        <text x="324" y="156">index -&gt; translate</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Which service is doing the work at each hop. -->
      <g class="node-label">
        <text x="0" y="192">document extraction</text>
        <text x="310" y="192">translation</text>
      </g>
      <g class="edge-label">
        <text x="0" y="212">increments the index</text>
        <text x="310" y="212">reads its own next task</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Only the index moves, so a message carries its own remaining itinerary and no service needs to know
    what follows it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
